From: Ely Office
Subject: Writer hides tracked deletions while marking insertions

- With track changes on, deleted text should leave the line at once
  and the rest reflow (#143), as in Word's Simple Markup. The margin
  mode moves deletions out of the body, which splits a run of deletes
  into several changes, so it is not used.
- The root frame gains a choice, HideTrackedDeletions: when changes
  are shown, the layout hides them as in the Final view, and the
  redline iterator still colours insertions in that mode.
- ShowTrackedChanges reports what the user picked, not the layout's
  hiding, and LOK reports HideTrackedDeletions.
- A paragraph whose deletion is not merged yet keeps the shown mode
  until the layout merges it, as the hiding iterator needs the merge.
- Saving to ODF, DOCX or DOC and the PDF export take shown changes
  from the user's pick too, so a save keeps the file in Markup.
- LOK redline notifications skip text rectangles while the layout hides
  changes: a merged paragraph learns of an erase only afterwards, and
  formatting it in between runs away (an ODF save erases every deletion).

